## Phase 6: Alternative schedule exploration

## Candidate 10: forall[4,4] + no K outer + [4,8,8] single-level + vectorize + unroll_K×8
- Schedule: forall[4,4] → tile_for [4,8,8] → vectorize → unroll×8 (no separate K outer)
- Time: 1.877 ms | WORSE
- Root cause: no K outer → A slice is 128×512=4MB per thread, overwhelms L2 cache
- Confirms: K outer=32 is essential for L1 locality

## Candidate 11: forall[4,4] + K[32] + [4,8,8] + vectorize + unroll_K×4 + unroll_mloop×2
- Added M inner loop unroll ×2 after K unroll (M loop: 128/4=32 iters → 16 after unroll)
- Time: 1.510 ms | WORSE (M unroll increases code size / register pressure)

## Candidate 12: forall[8,4] + K[32] + [4,8,8] + vectorize + unroll_K×4
- Changed forall from [4,4] (16 threads, M=128/N=128) to [8,4] (32 threads, M=64/N=128)
- A_tile=64×32=16KB (under L1), B_tile=32×128=32KB (at L1 boundary)
- Time: 1.313 ms | Slightly WORSE than [4,4]
- Confirms: [4,4] = 16 threads with square 128×128 per-thread tile is optimal for 512×512

## Candidate 13: forall[4,4] + K[32] + [4,8,4] + vectorize + unroll_K×8
- Smaller K_inner=4, vector<4x8x4xf64>=128 elements, 8 fully-unrolled copies
- Time: 1.556 ms | WORSE (more unroll copies with smaller vectors = more overhead)

### Phase 6 Summary
- None of: no-K-outer, M-unroll, [8,4] threads, smaller K-inner improve over C7
- Best remains C7: 1.299 ms

---

## FINAL SUMMARY

- **BEST**: Candidate 7 — 1.299 ms
- Schedule: forall[4,4] num_threads + tile_for [0,0,32] (K outer) + tile_for [4,8,8] (register) + vectorize [4,8,8] + unroll_K×4
- Vectors: vector<4x8x8xf64> = 256 elements (well within 512-element limit)
- Speedup vs baseline (346.641ms): **266.9x**
- Speedup vs PyTorch (0.39196ms): **0.302x (3.3x slower)**

### Key Learnings for matmul_512_512_512
- Square matrix benefits from square thread distribution: [4,4] (16 threads) beats [4,8], [8,4] (32 threads)
- K outer=32 is optimal: A_tile=128×32=32KB and B_tile=32×128=32KB BOTH fit in L1 (32KB each)
- K outer=64 overflows L1; K outer=16 has too much loop overhead
- Inner tile [4,8,8] (vector<4x8x8xf64>=256 elem) beats [8,8,8] (512 elem) and [4,8,16] (512 elem)
  - Smaller vector reduces register pressure for square computation
- K inner unroll×4 is full unroll (32/8=4 iterations) — optimal
- Adding further unrolls (M×2, N×2, kloop1×2) all worse
- 3-level K tiling same or worse than 2-level K=32
- No-K-outer schedule is much worse (A tile spills from L2)
- Default bufferization pipeline (innerparallel + full_unroll=true) is CRITICAL
- Performance wall: 3.3× from PyTorch due to MKL micro-kernels + prefetching + Turbo boost
